If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder then an opioid-use-disorder-counseling can possibly benefit the patient.
If a clinician offers an opioid-use-disorder-counseling to a patient then it is recommended that the clinician does not replace an evidence-based-medication-treatment for the patient with the opioid-use-disorder-counseling.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder then a mutual-help-group-referral can possibly benefit the patient.
If a clinician offers a mutual-help-group-referral to a patient then it is recommended that the clinician does not replace an evidence-based-medication-treatment for the patient with the mutual-help-group-referral.
A mutual-help-group-referral-example is a Narcotics-Anonymous-referral-example.
